INSERT INTO posts (id, title, slug, kicker, category, accent, excerpt, lead, content, cover_url, author, tags, meta_title, meta_description, read_time_minutes, published, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('954e55e0-330d-482e-a8dd-f8ace17f2dbd', 'How to Keep Your Home Allergen-Free: A Cleaning Guide', 'allergen-free-home-cleaning-guide', 'Health & Wellness', 'Health & Home', 'pink', 'Dust mites, pet dander and pollen build up fast in Pacific Northwest homes. Here''s the cleaning routine that actually reduces allergens — backed by what we see in hundreds of Seattle-area homes.', 'If you wake up congested or your allergies flare indoors, your home''s surfaces are probably holding more allergens than you think. The good news: a consistent cleaning routine measurably reduces dust mites, pet dander and pollen — here''s the one that works.', '## Where allergens actually live

Allergens concentrate in soft surfaces and low-airflow zones: mattresses and bedding, upholstered furniture, carpets and rugs, curtains, and the tops of shelves and ceiling fans where dust settles and recirculates every time the heat kicks on.

## The weekly routine that makes a difference

1. Vacuum carpets and upholstery with a HEPA-filter vacuum — standard bags recirculate fine particles right back into the air.
2. Wash bedding in hot water — warm water doesn''t kill dust mites; hot water does.
3. Damp-dust surfaces — dry dusting just relocates allergens. A damp microfiber cloth traps them.
4. Wipe window sills and tracks — Seattle''s long pollen season deposits buildup you rarely notice.

## Monthly: go deeper

Rotate in the tasks that soft surfaces need: vacuum the mattress itself, wash curtains, wipe ceiling fan blades and exhaust fan grills, and clean under beds and sofas where dust bunnies feed the cycle.

## Pets and allergies can coexist

Dander sticks to every fabric in the house, so frequency is everything: homes with shedding pets need vacuuming two to three times a week. All the products our teams use are pet-safe and non-toxic — a question we get so often we answer it in every quote.

> "We use professional-grade, non-toxic, biodegradable products safe for children, pets, and clients with allergies or sensitivities."
> — Cleaning Paradise Team

## When professional deep cleaning helps

A [professional deep clean](/cleaning-services-in-wa/deep-cleaning) resets your home''s allergen load — extracting what''s settled deep in carpets, behind furniture, and in the corners weekly routines don''t reach. Many of our clients with allergies schedule one seasonally, with standard cleaning in between.

Breathing easier is a quote away: [contact Cleaning Paradise](/contact) and tell us about your home — we serve the greater Seattle area, Mon–Sat.', 'https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785854820554-8hfu19p7w7g.webp', 'Cleaning Paradise Team', '["Allergies","Health","Deep Clean","Pets"]', 'How to Reduce Allergens at Home: Cleaning Guide for Seattle Homes', 'The cleaning routine that actually reduces dust mites, pet dander and pollen at home. Weekly and monthly checklists, plus when a professional deep clean helps.', 1, 1, '2026-07-08T00:00:00+00:00', '2026-07-23T02:28:14.142529+00:00', '2026-08-04T14:48:48.638+00:00');

INSERT INTO posts (id, title, slug, kicker, category, accent, excerpt, lead, content, cover_url, author, tags, meta_title, meta_description, read_time_minutes, published, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('21da5b37-87de-47f1-a466-754eff2dbbde', 'Move-Out Cleaning Checklist: Get Your Full Deposit Back', 'move-out-cleaning-checklist-deposit', 'Moving Guide', 'Moving Tips', 'blue', 'The room-by-room checklist landlords and property managers actually inspect — and the commonly missed spots that cost renters part of their deposit.', 'Moving is stressful enough without losing part of your security deposit to a failed final inspection. This is the checklist Seattle-area landlords and property managers actually use — plus the spots renters miss most often.', '## What landlords actually inspect

Property managers don''t walk in with fresh eyes — they walk in with a checklist and photos from your move-in date. The standard they expect is "ready for the next tenant," which is closer to a professional deep clean than a weekend tidy-up.

## Kitchen: the deposit killer

1. Inside the oven — baked-on grease is the single most common deduction.
2. Inside the fridge and freezer — defrosted, wiped, and left open to air.
3. Behind appliances — pull the stove and fridge out; crumbs and grease build up on the floor and walls.
4. Cabinets and drawers — empty, wiped inside and out, handles degreased.
5. Sink and faucet — descaled and polished.

## Bathrooms: where grime hides

Scrub grout lines, descale the showerhead, polish mirrors and chrome, and wipe down the exhaust fan grill. If there''s visible mold on caulk, address it — inspectors photograph it every time.

## The commonly missed spots

- Baseboards and door frames
- Window tracks and interior glass
- Light fixtures and ceiling fan blades
- Closet shelving
- Wall scuffs (a magic eraser handles most)

## When to book professionals instead

If you''re juggling boxes, utilities and a new address, a professional [move in / out cleaning](/cleaning-services-in-wa/move-in-out) pays for itself — it''s typically far cheaper than the deduction a failed inspection brings. Our teams clean to inspection standard: appliances inside and out, baseboards, windows, and every spot on this list.

Moving within King or Snohomish County? [Get a free move-out cleaning quote](/contact) and we''ll reply within one business day — we serve [Seattle, Bellevue, Kirkland, Lynnwood and surrounding cities](/locations).', 'https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785855106293-e3zqtwweaqi.webp', 'Cleaning Paradise Team', '["Move Out Cleaning","Checklist","Renters","Deposit"]', 'Move-Out Cleaning Checklist for Renters (Get Your Deposit Back)', 'Room-by-room move-out cleaning checklist Seattle landlords actually inspect. What renters miss most — and when to book professional move-out cleaning.', 1, 1, '2026-06-24T00:00:00+00:00', '2026-07-23T02:28:14.142529+00:00', '2026-08-04T14:53:42.641+00:00');

INSERT INTO posts (id, title, slug, kicker, category, accent, excerpt, lead, content, cover_url, author, tags, meta_title, meta_description, read_time_minutes, published, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('df5d9b7f-5888-4d75-bebe-0e25b3895f66', 'How to Deep Clean Your Home This Spring', 'how-to-deep-clean-your-home-this-spring', 'Spring Cleaning Guide', 'Cleaning Tips', 'pink', 'A complete checklist for refreshing every room of your home as the season changes. From windows to baseboards, we break it down into manageable steps.', 'Spring is the perfect moment to press reset on your home. After months of closed windows and indoor living, a thorough deep clean removes built-up grime, freshens the air, and gives every room a new lease on life.', '## Start with a plan, room by room

Jumping in without a structure is the fastest way to feel overwhelmed and leave things half-done. Break your home into zones: kitchen, bathrooms, bedrooms, living areas, and overlooked spaces (garage, laundry room, entryway). Tackle one zone per day and you''ll finish the whole house in a week without exhausting yourself.

Write the list down. Checking off tasks gives you real momentum and keeps you from skipping the zones that feel less urgent (baseboards, we''re looking at you).

> "A clean home isn''t just about appearances, it''s about the feeling you get walking in through the door."  
> — Cleaning Paradise Team

![SPRING~1 (1).webp](https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785860626604-9yisn6yhqfq.webp)

## The kitchen: where grease hides

The kitchen accumulates grease in places you rarely notice until you''re doing a proper deep clean. Here''s what most people miss:

1. The range hood filter, remove it, soak in hot soapy water for 15 minutes, scrub, rinse.
2. Behind and under appliances, pull out the fridge and stove to wipe down walls, coils, and floors.
3. Cabinet doors and handles, use a degreaser, not just an all-purpose cleaner.
4. Dishwasher interior, run an empty cycle with a cup of white vinegar on the top rack.

## Bathrooms: beyond the obvious

Most people regularly clean the toilet bowl, sink, and mirror, but spring cleaning means going further. Scrub grout with a stiff brush and a paste of baking soda and water. Clean showerhead buildup by tying a bag of white vinegar around it overnight. Replace the shower liner if it has visible mold.

Don''t forget exhaust fans, they accumulate dust that gets recirculated into the air you breathe. Use a vacuum brush attachment to clean the grill, then wipe it down.

## When to call in the professionals

A DIY spring clean handles a lot, but some tasks are better left to trained teams with the right equipment. Carpet deep cleaning, upholstery extraction, high-reach window cleaning, and post-renovation cleanup all benefit from professional-grade tools and solutions that aren''t available over the counter.

At Cleaning Paradise, we offer a dedicated Spring Deep Clean package that covers your entire home in a single visit, including all the zones most homeowners skip. We bring everything needed; you just enjoy the result.', 'https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785860727808-4uod8lnrrdb.webp', 'Cleaning Paradise Team', '["Spring Cleaning","Deep Clean","Home Tips","Greater Seattle"]', 'Spring Deep Cleaning Guide for Seattle Homes | Room by Room', 'A room by room spring deep cleaning checklist for Seattle homes, plus the tasks worth leaving to the pros. Get a free quote from Cleaning Paradise.', 2, 1, '2026-03-15T00:00:00+00:00', '2026-07-23T02:03:33.332651+00:00', '2026-08-04T16:27:04.887+00:00');

INSERT INTO posts (id, title, slug, kicker, category, accent, excerpt, lead, content, cover_url, author, tags, meta_title, meta_description, read_time_minutes, published, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('ab17945f-ec8e-400a-bd01-e1e540137675', 'Why a Clean Office Is Worth More Than It Costs', 'cleenefitsan-office-professional-cleaning-b', 'Workplace', 'Commercial', 'blue', 'Sick days, client first impressions, and employee morale all trace back to how clean your workspace is. What commercial cleaning actually changes — and what to look for in a provider.', 'Your office says something before anyone in it speaks. For clients, it''s credibility. For employees, it''s whether the company cares. And for your budget, the math on professional cleaning is more favorable than most managers assume.', '## The hidden cost of a dirty office

Shared desks, door handles, break-room surfaces and keyboards are germ superhighways. Offices that skip professional disinfection see it show up where it hurts: sick days. A single flu cycle moving through a small team costs more in lost productivity than months of cleaning service.

## First impressions are inventory

Clients notice floors, glass, restrooms and smells — in that order, and within seconds. None of it appears in your pitch deck, and all of it affects whether you look like a business that handles details.

## What professional commercial cleaning covers

1. Daily-touch disinfection — handles, switches, shared equipment, break areas.
2. Restrooms to a standard employees notice — stocked, sanitized, odor-free.
3. Floors and glass — entryways, conference rooms, and the windows everyone sees from the street.
4. Scheduled deep cleans — carpets, upholstery and vents on a monthly or quarterly rotation.

## What to look for in a provider

Licensed, insured and bonded — non-negotiable for anyone with keys to your space. Consistent crews, so quality doesn''t reset every visit. And flexible scheduling: evening and early-morning service means your team never works around a vacuum.

## Right-sized for small business

You don''t need a corporate janitorial contract. Our [commercial cleaning service](/cleaning-services-in-wa/commercial-cleaning) covers offices, studios and retail across the greater Seattle area with the same teams and standards as our residential service — scheduled around your hours, Mon–Sat.

[Request a free walkthrough quote](/contact) — tell us your square footage and schedule, and we''ll reply within one business day.', 'https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785854022621-blydv9jqgpk.webp', 'Cleaning Paradise Team', '["Commercial Cleaning","Office","Small Business","Productivity"]', 'Why Professional Office Cleaning Pays for Itself | Seattle, WA', 'Fewer sick days, better first impressions, higher morale: what commercial cleaning changes for small offices, and what to look for in a Seattle provider.', 1, 1, '2026-07-15T00:00:00+00:00', '2026-07-23T02:28:14.142529+00:00', '2026-08-04T14:35:23.76+00:00');

INSERT INTO posts (id, title, slug, kicker, category, accent, excerpt, lead, content, cover_url, author, tags, meta_title, meta_description, read_time_minutes, published, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('6a8919de-0aa7-430a-a559-f102cd15a791', 'How to Prepare Your Pets for Cleaning Day in Seattle', 'prepare-pets-cleaning-day-seattle', 'Pet Friendly Home Care', 'Health & Home', 'pink', 'Dogs and cats notice everything, especially a new team at the door. Here is a simple way to keep your pet calm and safe while your Seattle home gets cleaned.', 'Booking a house cleaning service in Seattle should feel like a relief, not a stressful morning for your dog or cat. Pets read every change in the house, from the sound of a vacuum to the smell of a fresh product. With a few small steps before our team arrives, cleaning day becomes calm for everyone, including the furry members of your family.', '### Give your pet a quiet room

The easiest step is also the most effective. Pick one room our team will not need to enter, or that we can clean first, and set it up as your pet safe zone. Add their bed, water, a favorite toy and something that smells like you. Close the door and add a note so everyone knows the room is occupied. This works for anxious dogs, senior cats and any pet that reacts to strangers.

### Tell us about your pet when you book

When you request your free quote, let us know how many pets you have, their names and how they usually behave with visitors. Our professional cleaners in Seattle adjust their routine when they know a cat likes to slip out the front door or a dog gets nervous around the vacuum. Small details make a big difference in the final result.

### Secure doors, gates and windows

Open doors are the number one risk on cleaning day. Before we arrive, check that gates in the yard are locked and that your pet is wearing an updated ID tag. If you use a microchip, confirm your contact information is current. Our housekeeping team keeps entries closed, but a second layer of protection is always smart.

### Pick up toys, bowls and bedding

Clearing the floor lets our team reach every corner and clean faster. Move food bowls to a counter, gather chew toys into a basket and shake out pet beds. If a blanket needs a wash, leave it in the laundry area and let us know. Less clutter means a deeper clean in the same visit.

### Ask for products that are safe around animals

Many families in Seattle, Bellevue, Kirkland and Lynnwood want a home that is fresh without heavy chemical smells. We work with eco friendly and low odor products that are gentle around pets and kids, and we always ventilate while we work. If your pet has allergies or a sensitive stomach, tell us and we will adapt the products we use in your home.

### Plan the rest of the day

After the service, keep your pet in their safe room for about twenty minutes while floors dry and the air settles. Then let them explore. Most dogs go straight to sniffing every clean surface, which is a very good sign.

### Cleaning day should feel easy

A pet friendly home cleaning service in Seattle is not only about the shine. It is about walking in at the end of the day and finding your house calm, fresh and safe for everyone who lives there.

Ready to book your next visit? [Get your free quote](#cotizar) or explore our [cleaning services](/services) and the [areas we serve](/locations) across King and Snohomish Counties.', 'https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785854229325-yaf621e8bf9.webp', 'Cleaning Paradise Team', '["pet friendly cleaning","house cleaning Seattle","cleaning services Seattle","maid service Seattle","eco friendly cleaning","pet owners","home care tips","Bellevue","Kirkland","Lynnwood"]', 'Pet Friendly House Cleaning in Seattle: How to Prepare Your Pets', 'Simple steps to prepare your dog or cat before your house cleaning service in Seattle arrives. Safe rooms, secure doors and pet friendly products. Get a free quote.', 2, 1, '2026-08-04T01:09:09.727+00:00', '2026-08-04T01:10:46.819699+00:00', '2026-08-04T14:38:49.299+00:00');

INSERT INTO posts (id, title, slug, kicker, category, accent, excerpt, lead, content, cover_url, author, tags, meta_title, meta_description, read_time_minutes, published, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('ed260908-de76-44e3-a69f-de163e7c1b4b', 'How Much Does House Cleaning Cost in Seattle? (2026 Guide)', 'house-cleaning-cost-seattle', 'Pricing Guide', 'Cleaning Tips', 'pink', 'What actually determines the price of a house cleaning in the Seattle area — home size, condition, frequency — and how to get an accurate quote without surprises.', 'If you''ve searched "house cleaning cost near me," you''ve probably found wildly different numbers. That''s because honest pricing depends on your specific home. Here''s how professional cleaning is actually priced in the Seattle area — and how to get a real number for your home in minutes.', '## Why there''s no one-size-fits-all price

Two 2-bedroom homes can take wildly different amounts of time to clean. A tidy apartment that gets professional attention every two weeks is a different job than a home that hasn''t had a deep clean in a year. That''s why reputable cleaning companies quote per home, not from a flat rate card.

## The four factors that determine your price

1. Home size, bedrooms, bathrooms, and total square footage set the baseline amount of work.
2. Current condition, a first-time or long-overdue clean takes longer than maintaining an already-clean home.
3. Type of service, standard maintenance cleaning, [deep cleaning](/cleaning-services-in-wa/deep-cleaning), or move in / move out cleaning each involve different checklists.
4. Frequency, weekly and biweekly clients pay less per visit than one-time cleanings, because the home stays in better shape between visits.

## Recurring service: where the real savings are

The most cost-effective way to keep a spotless home is a recurring schedule. After an initial deep clean brings every room up to standard, biweekly or monthly maintenance visits are faster, and priced accordingly. Most of our Seattle-area clients land on biweekly service as the sweet spot between cost and consistency.

> "Getting that quote is fast and free, no guessing, no surprises when the invoice arrives."  
> — Cleaning Paradise Team

## Watch out for quotes that seem too good

A suspiciously low flat rate usually means one of three things: the crew will rush, "extras" like ovens and baseboards will cost more on arrival, or the company isn''t licensed, insured and bonded. Always confirm all three before letting anyone into your home, we wrote about what that protects you from in our service pages.

## Get your exact number

The fastest way to find out what your home costs to clean is to [request a free quote](/contact), tell us your home''s size, condition, and how often you''d like us to come, and we''ll reply within one business day with a custom price. First-time clients get 30% off their first clean.', 'https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785859860393-onyh8roc4sj.webp', 'Cleaning Paradise Team', '["Pricing","House Cleaning","Seattle","Cost Guide"]', 'How Much Does House Cleaning Cost in Seattle, WA? (2026)', 'What determines house cleaning prices in Seattle: home size, condition, service type and frequency. Get a free custom quote from Cleaning Paradise.', 2, 1, '2026-06-10T00:00:00+00:00', '2026-07-23T02:28:14.142529+00:00', '2026-08-04T16:12:43.959+00:00');

INSERT INTO posts (id, title, slug, kicker, category, accent, excerpt, lead, content, cover_url, author, tags, meta_title, meta_description, read_time_minutes, published, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('f11a4ca2-88ed-419e-ad57-e4d02695fd3c', 'What a Commercial Cleaning Company Should Do for Your Seattle Business', 'commercial-cleaning-company-seattle', 'Workspace Standards', 'Commercial', 'pink', 'Your workspace is the first thing clients notice and the last thing your team stops noticing. Here is what professional commercial cleaning covers, who needs it most, and how to tell a serious company from the rest.
', 'A clean workspace is not decoration. It is part of how your business is judged, how your team performs, and how long your floors and furniture last. Still, most owners in the Seattle area only think about commercial cleaning when something goes wrong: a client comments on the restroom, the carpet starts to smell, or the office manager quits doing a job that was never theirs. Here is what a professional commercial cleaning company should actually deliver, so you know what to ask for before you sign anything.', '## Why it matters more than most owners think

Dust, sticky door handles and overflowing bins send a message to every client who walks in, and they send an even louder one to your team. People work better in spaces that feel cared for. Shared keyboards, elevator buttons, breakroom counters and restroom fixtures are the surfaces that move illness through an office fastest, which turns cleaning into a staffing issue as much as an appearance one. Your workspace is a physical version of your brand, and clients read it in the first ten seconds.

**What commercial cleaning actually covers**

A real commercial program is not a vacuum and a trash run. It should include:

1. Floor care, vacuuming, mopping and sanitation appropriate to the surface, whether that is carpet, vinyl, tile or hardwood.
2. Dusting at every level, from desks and monitors down to baseboards and up to vents and light fixtures.
3. Disinfection of high touch surfaces, door handles, switches, shared equipment, railings and restroom fixtures.
4. Restrooms and breakrooms held to a fixed standard, not to whoever noticed last.
5. A janitorial schedule built around your hours, nightly, several times a week, or weekly, with deeper resets on a rotation.

**Who needs it most**

Office administrators, retail managers, clinic staff and business owners across Seattle, Bellevue, Kirkland, Lynnwood and Shoreline all share the same problem: cleaning is everyone''s job until it is nobody''s. If your space sees customers, if you have more than a handful of employees, or if someone on payroll is quietly wiping counters between real tasks, you are already paying for cleaning. You are just paying for it in the least efficient way possible.

**How to tell a serious company from the rest**

Three questions separate a professional from a risk:

1. **Are you licensed, insured and bonded?** If anything is damaged or anyone is injured in your space, this is the only thing standing between you and the bill. Ask to see it, not just hear it.
2. **What products do you use?** Offices with staff who have allergies or sensitivities need low odor and eco friendly solutions, not a chemical smell that lingers into Monday morning.
3. **Can you work around our hours?** Cleaning during business hours interrupts your operation. A capable team works evenings, early mornings or weekends so your staff walks into a finished space.

![COMMER~1.webp](https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785863594758-vxdv33ivrre.webp)

**What about the cost**

Commercial cleaning is quoted per space, never from a flat rate card, because square footage, foot traffic, surface types and frequency all change the work involved. Higher frequency usually lowers the cost per visit, since a maintained space takes less time than a neglected one. We walk your space, then quote it. You can read more about how cleaning is priced in our [cost guide.](https://cleaning-paradise.nexteralab.workers.dev/blog/house-cleaning-cost-seattle)

## Quick answers

**How much does commercial cleaning cost?**

It depends on the size and condition of your space, the services you need and how often you need them. We provide a custom quote after seeing the space, with no surprise charges added later.

**Are your cleaners bonded and insured?**

Yes. Cleaning Paradise is licensed, insured and bonded, and every team member is vetted before entering a client property.

**Can you clean after hours?**

Yes. We build schedules around your operating hours, including evenings and weekends, so your business never pauses for a cleaning crew.

**Build a plan around your space**

Every business has a different rhythm. A retail floor on a Saturday and a quiet clinic on a Tuesday do not need the same thing. Tell us how your space is used and we will build a maintenance plan that fits it.

[Contact our commercial cleaning team](https://cleaning-paradise.nexteralab.workers.dev/contact) for a free custom quote, or see everything included in our [commercial cleaning service.](https://cleaning-paradise.nexteralab.workers.dev/cleaning-services-in-wa/commercial-cleaning)

', 'https://hzltqqipoimexejgcpuo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1785863671111-z7hmym5v4jf.jpg', 'Cleaning Paradise Team', '["commercial cleaning","office cleaning","janitorial services","Seattle","King County","business tips","disinfection"]', 'Commercial Cleaning Company in Seattle: What to Expect', 'What professional commercial cleaning covers, who needs it, and the three questions to ask before hiring in Seattle. Get a free custom quote for your business.', 3, 1, '2026-08-04T17:13:21.961+00:00', '2026-08-04T17:14:54.584908+00:00', '2026-08-04T17:16:16.44+00:00');

INSERT INTO posts (id, title, slug, kicker, category, accent, excerpt, lead, content, cover_url, author, tags, meta_title, meta_description, read_time_minutes, published, published_at, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bf714ab4-8fcb-4422-8c76-89d90cf9df95', 'How to Remove Carpet Stains Without Damaging Your Fibers', 'how-to-remove-carpet-stains', 'Carpet Care Basics', 'Cleaning Tips', 'pink', 'Most carpet stains are easy to fix if you act fast and use the right method. Here is what works at home, what ruins carpet for good, and when to call a pro.', 'Something spills. You grab a towel, you scrub, and the stain gets bigger. This happens to almost everyone. The good news is that most carpet stains come out just fine when you know what to do in the first few minutes. The bad news is that a few common tricks people find online can damage your carpet forever. Here is a simple guide to both.', '## Why stains stick in the first place

Carpet fibers are not flat. Up close they look like tiny ropes with open spaces between them. When you spill something, the liquid slides down those spaces and sits at the base, where you cannot see it.

Stains fall into three simple groups, and each one behaves differently:

1. **Sugar and food stains.** Juice, soda, coffee and wine. These dry into a sticky layer that grabs dirt. The spot looks darker over time because it is collecting dust, not because the stain is spreading.
2. **Oil and grease stains.** Butter, makeup, lotion. Water alone will not touch these. Oil and water do not mix, so you need a little soap to break the oil apart.
3. **Protein stains.** Milk, blood, pet accidents. These are the tricky ones. Hot water cooks protein and locks it into the fiber. Always use cold water on these.

Knowing which group you are dealing with saves you a lot of guessing.

### Three rules that matter more than any product

**Act fast.** A fresh spill sits on top of the fiber. After a few hours it soaks into the backing underneath. Fresh spills are easy. Old spills are a project.

**Blot, never rub.** Rubbing pushes the spill deeper and breaks the fiber, which leaves a rough, fuzzy patch that stays visible even after the color is gone. Press a clean white cloth straight down, lift, move to a dry part of the cloth, and repeat.

**Work from the outside in.** Start at the edge of the spot and move toward the center. If you start in the middle, you push the stain outward and make it wider.

## Safe things you can try at home

For most fresh, light stains, this is all you need:

- **Cold water and a clean cloth.** Try this first. A surprising number of fresh spills come out with nothing else.
- **A drop of clear dish soap in a cup of cold water.** Good for food and grease. Use very little soap. Too much leaves a sticky film that attracts dirt and makes the spot come back darker.
- **White vinegar mixed half and half with water.** Good for coffee, tea and light pet spots. Let it sit for five minutes, then blot.
- **Baking soda.** Sprinkle it on a damp spot, let it dry fully, then vacuum. It pulls out moisture and smell.

Two habits to build. First, always test your mix on a hidden corner, like inside a closet, and wait ten minutes to see if the color changes. Second, use as little liquid as possible. Soaking the carpet pushes the stain into the padding below, where it can grow mold and come back weeks later.

### **When to stop and put the bottle down**

Some things do real damage, and once the damage is done, the only fix is replacing the carpet. Do not use these:

- **Bleach or any product with bleach in it.** It strips the color out permanently and leaves a pale patch.
- **Ammonia on wool carpet.** Wool is a natural fiber and ammonia breaks it down.
- **Hot water on milk, blood or pet accidents.** Heat sets protein stains for good.
- **Stiff brushes or scrubbing.** This shreds the fiber tips. The spot will look worn even after it is clean.
- **Rust removers, hair dye removers or paint thinner.** These are far too strong for carpet.

Also stop if the stain is older than a few days, larger than your hand, on wool or silk, or if you have already tried two things that did not work. At that point, more attempts usually make it worse.

> If you are at that point, do not risk it. Take a look at our [carpet cleaning service](https://claude.ai/cleaning-services-in-wa/carpet-cleaning) and let a trained team handle it.

### **Why professional steam extraction works better**

Home methods clean the top of the fiber. That is why a stain can look gone and then reappear a week later. What happened is simple. The stain was never removed. It was pushed down into the backing, and as the carpet dried, it traveled back up to the surface.

Steam extraction, sometimes called hot water extraction, works differently. Hot water and a cleaning solution go into the carpet under pressure, they loosen everything sitting at the base of the fiber, and then a strong vacuum pulls the water back out along with the dirt. The carpet is cleaned all the way down and it dries quickly, usually in a few hours.

Two things make this safer than renting a machine and doing it yourself. A trained team knows how much moisture your specific carpet can take, and professional machines pull far more water back out. Leaving a carpet too wet is one of the most common ways people damage their own floors.

### **Pet stains need a different approach**

Pet accidents are not just a stain. They are a smell problem, and the smell is what brings pets back to the same spot.

Regular cleaners cover the odor for a few days. They do not remove the source, which is soaked into the padding under the carpet. Professional pet treatment uses enzyme cleaners, which are solutions that break down the material causing the smell instead of masking it. Combined with extraction, this removes both the mark and the reason your pet keeps returning to that corner.

If you have pets, you may also like our guide on [how to get your pets ready for cleaning day.](https://claude.ai/blog/prepare-pets-cleaning-day-seattle)

### **Get it done right**

Fresh spills are yours. Old stains, pet odor and anything on wool are ours. If you are looking at a spot you have already tried to fix, stop before it becomes permanent.

